Package: ranypia
Title: Social Security Benefit-Formula Functions, Penny-Exact with SSA's AnyPIA
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Anthony", "Colavito", email = "colavitoanthony@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Vectorized functions for the Social Security benefit formula:
    average indexed monthly earnings, the primary insurance amount, the
    family maximum, cost-of-living adjustments, claiming-age reductions and
    credits, insured status, the special minimum, and spouse, child and
    survivor benefits. Results match the Social Security Administration's
    Detailed Calculator (AnyPIA, 2026 Trustees Report) to the cent. An R
    port of the Python package 'pyanypia', built for hypothetical examples
    and microsimulation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/anthonycolavito/ranypia
BugReports: https://github.com/anthonycolavito/ranypia/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    rlang,
    tibble,
    tidyr
Suggests:
    dplyr,
    jsonlite,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
